recording makes ZERO provider calls -- safe to re-run after a crash, a code change, or just to look
again. Keyed per model, so widening the ensemble costs only the widening; otherwise nobody would
ever add the second model, and agreement between independent readings is the strongest signal this
pipeline produces without a human.
Failure is PARTIAL, never total: one dead provider must not lose the answers that arrived. But
TOTAL failure refuses rather than persisting an empty analysis, because an empty analysis on disk
reads as "we watched it and found nothing" -- the opposite of what happened.
